The attached image, Figure 5 from the 2015 paper, illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles significantly enhance the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A's dot plots show that soluble ovalbumin (OVA) alone is minimally internalized, but when adsorbed to Nano-11 ("Nano-11+OVA"), there is a substantial increase in cells positive for both Nano-11 and OVA fluorescence, indicating efficient co-delivery. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, quantifies this effect, with the "Nano-11+OVA" curve exhibiting a pronounced rightward shift, demonstrating a much higher amount of OVA internalized per cell compared to soluble OVA, thus enhancing antigen delivery to DCs.